From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:56:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hwmon: macsmc: Print voltage and current keys in the
 debugfs key list

The debugfs key list prints a value only for temperature (T*) and
power (P*) float keys. The PMU rail voltage (V*) and current (I*)
keys, such as VP0b and IP0b for the P-cluster rail, end the line at
the flags byte, so a tool that takes the last field reads the flags
(0x85) as the value.

Read V* and I* float keys too, scaled by 1000 like the others, so
they show in mV and mA. Per-rail voltage under load can then be read
next to the power keys without a separate tool.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.c b/drivers/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.c
index 5a264c9d2e..97d4fd76cb 100644
--- a/drivers/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.c
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.c
@@ -1470,7 +1470,7 @@ static int macsmc_hwmon_keys_show(struct seq_file *m, void *unused)
 	u32 i;
 	int ret;
 
-	seq_printf(m, "# %u keys: index key type size flags [value: T* in mC, P* in mW]\n",
+	seq_printf(m, "# %u keys: index key type size flags [value: T* mC, P* mW, V* mV, I* mA]\n",
 		   smc->key_count);
 	for (i = 0; i < smc->key_count; i++) {
 		if (fatal_signal_pending(current))
@@ -1492,7 +1492,8 @@ static int macsmc_hwmon_keys_show(struct seq_file *m, void *unused)
 		seq_printf(m, " %3u %02x", info.size, info.flags);
 		if (info.type_code == __SMC_KEY('f', 'l', 't', ' ') && info.size == sizeof(u32) &&
 		    (info.flags & APPLE_SMC_READABLE) &&
-		    ((key >> 24) == 'T' || (key >> 24) == 'P')) {
+		    ((key >> 24) == 'T' || (key >> 24) == 'P' ||
+		     (key >> 24) == 'V' || (key >> 24) == 'I')) {
 			ret = macsmc_hwmon_read_f32_scaled(smc, key, &value, 1000);
 			if (ret < 0)
 				seq_printf(m, " read error %d", ret);
-- 
